WEBVTT

00:00:00.442 --> 00:00:03.153
Last video ended here, with F of x

00:00:03.314 --> 00:00:05.101
equals x squared over nine.

00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:06.577
Let's give it a meaning.

00:00:07.325 --> 00:00:09.655
A parcel tracker says your delivery will come

00:00:09.697 --> 00:00:11.062
between nine and twelve.

00:00:11.925 --> 00:00:14.148
X is the arrival time in hours after

00:00:14.189 --> 00:00:16.352
nine, and F of x is the chance

00:00:16.413 --> 00:00:17.995
the parcel has arrived by then.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.155
F climbs slowly near zero, and steeply near

00:00:22.256 --> 00:00:22.537
three.

00:00:23.402 --> 00:00:25.773
Compare two strips of the same width, a

00:00:25.854 --> 00:00:26.678
tenth of an hour.

00:00:27.482 --> 00:00:29.765
From zero point five to zero point six,

00:00:30.307 --> 00:00:32.891
F only rises by about zero point zero

00:00:33.052 --> 00:00:33.512
one two.

00:00:34.394 --> 00:00:36.380
From two point five to two point six,

00:00:36.823 --> 00:00:39.331
it rises by about zero point zero five

00:00:39.432 --> 00:00:39.692
seven.

00:00:40.355 --> 00:00:43.180
So the same width holds almost five times

00:00:43.282 --> 00:00:45.505
as much probability near two point five.

00:00:46.651 --> 00:00:49.265
Steep means the arrival times are packed closely.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:51.477
So how do we measure that packing?

00:00:52.321 --> 00:00:54.504
Divide the rise in F by the width

00:00:54.564 --> 00:00:56.868
of the strip, and you get probability per

00:00:57.008 --> 00:00:59.092
unit of x, here per hour.

00:00:59.913 --> 00:01:02.199
Make the strip thinner and thinner, and that

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:03.824
becomes the gradient of F.

00:01:04.586 --> 00:01:07.111
So we define the probability density function, f

00:01:07.151 --> 00:01:09.876
of x, as F prime of x, wherever

00:01:10.156 --> 00:01:11.278
F has a gradient.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.368
Here, f of x is two x over

00:01:14.428 --> 00:01:17.719
nine, between zero and three, and zero everywhere

00:01:17.759 --> 00:01:17.900
else.

00:01:18.663 --> 00:01:19.605
At one point five,

00:01:20.208 --> 00:01:23.016
F has gradient one third, so the density

00:01:23.057 --> 00:01:24.802
there is one third per hour.

00:01:25.705 --> 00:01:27.273
A density isn't a probability.

00:01:27.636 --> 00:01:30.165
It's probability per unit of x, like a

00:01:30.247 --> 00:01:32.094
rope's density in grams per metre.

00:01:32.858 --> 00:01:35.446
A high density means probability is packed in

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:36.289
near that value,

00:01:36.873 --> 00:01:38.538
not that the exact value is likely.

00:01:39.162 --> 00:01:39.949
Here's why that matters.

00:01:40.453 --> 00:01:42.706
Go back to the reaction-time histogram from last

00:01:42.747 --> 00:01:43.109
video.

00:01:43.813 --> 00:01:46.245
Divide each relative frequency by the class width,

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:47.492
one tenth of a second.

00:01:48.276 --> 00:01:51.442
The heights become one, two point five, three

00:01:51.503 --> 00:01:53.486
point five, two and one,

00:01:53.988 --> 00:01:54.588
per second.

00:01:55.291 --> 00:01:58.141
Now each bar's area, height times width, is

00:01:58.202 --> 00:01:58.964
its probability,

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:00.851
and the areas add to one.

00:02:01.617 --> 00:02:03.590
Three point five is bigger than one, and

00:02:03.632 --> 00:02:04.114
that's fine.

00:02:04.518 --> 00:02:06.706
A density can be bigger than one, because

00:02:06.747 --> 00:02:09.418
the probability is the area, not the height.

00:02:10.249 --> 00:02:12.723
So for a density, probability is area.

00:02:13.669 --> 00:02:15.170
For the density models we use,

00:02:15.772 --> 00:02:17.153
F is a primitive of f,

00:02:18.356 --> 00:02:20.978
so the area under f from c to

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.442
d is F of d minus F of

00:02:23.563 --> 00:02:23.802
c.

00:02:24.705 --> 00:02:27.511
That's exactly the probability that X is between

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:28.393
c and d.

00:02:29.276 --> 00:02:31.539
For the parcel, the area under two x

00:02:31.681 --> 00:02:34.144
over nine from one to two is four

00:02:34.205 --> 00:02:36.869
ninths minus one ninth, which is one third.

00:02:37.612 --> 00:02:39.718
That's the chance it arrives between ten and

00:02:39.779 --> 00:02:42.708
eleven, the same one third last video found

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:43.371
from F.

00:02:44.214 --> 00:02:47.221
And since single values carry no probability, the

00:02:47.362 --> 00:02:48.965
ends of the interval still don't matter.

00:02:49.597 --> 00:02:51.310
Every density has two properties.

00:02:52.216 --> 00:02:55.064
First, f of x is never negative, because

00:02:55.386 --> 00:02:58.314
F never decreases, so its gradient can't be

00:02:58.335 --> 00:02:58.976
below zero.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.765
Second, the total area under f is one,

00:03:03.127 --> 00:03:04.669
because that's all of the probability.

00:03:05.432 --> 00:03:07.276
If X lives on an interval from a

00:03:07.337 --> 00:03:09.381
to b, the integral from a to b

00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:09.983
is one.

00:03:10.846 --> 00:03:12.812
If X can be any real number, the

00:03:12.873 --> 00:03:15.944
integral from minus infinity to infinity is one.

00:03:16.971 --> 00:03:18.204
Check two x over nine.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.337
It's never negative from zero to three, and

00:03:21.399 --> 00:03:22.782
its area is a triangle,

00:03:23.305 --> 00:03:25.631
half of three times two thirds, which is

00:03:25.832 --> 00:03:25.932
one.

00:03:26.635 --> 00:03:28.442
These two properties solve problems.

00:03:29.085 --> 00:03:31.766
A second courier's arrival time, X hours after

00:03:31.867 --> 00:03:35.188
eight, has density k times four minus x,

00:03:35.609 --> 00:03:37.750
for x from zero to four, and zero

00:03:37.851 --> 00:03:38.190
elsewhere.

00:03:38.974 --> 00:03:40.922
Their stop is early on the route, so

00:03:41.064 --> 00:03:42.711
early arrivals are most likely.

00:03:43.296 --> 00:03:43.799
Find k.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.503
The total area must be one.

00:03:47.127 --> 00:03:49.214
The graph is a triangle with base four

00:03:49.335 --> 00:03:51.904
and height four k, so its area is

00:03:51.925 --> 00:03:52.385
eight k.

00:03:53.129 --> 00:03:54.583
Integrating gives the same answer.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:57.877
So eight k equals one, and k is

00:03:58.039 --> 00:03:58.459
one eighth.

00:03:59.263 --> 00:04:00.909
It has to be positive, because a density

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:01.632
can't be negative.

00:04:02.215 --> 00:04:04.444
Now find the probability that X is less

00:04:04.485 --> 00:04:04.886
than one,

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.296
so this courier comes before nine.

00:04:08.041 --> 00:04:10.778
Integrate four minus x, over eight, from zero

00:04:10.859 --> 00:04:11.200
to one.

00:04:12.043 --> 00:04:14.324
That's one eighth of four minus a half,

00:04:14.705 --> 00:04:16.005
which is seven sixteenths.

00:04:16.928 --> 00:04:18.759
Just under half of the probability sits in

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.248
the first hour of the four.

00:04:21.236 --> 00:04:23.409
That fits, because this density is highest at

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:23.771
zero.

00:04:24.411 --> 00:04:26.027
We can also build F from f.

00:04:26.269 --> 00:04:29.055
F of x is the area under f

00:04:29.216 --> 00:04:30.719
from the start of the domain up to

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:31.060
x.

00:04:31.563 --> 00:04:31.722
So

00:04:32.326 --> 00:04:34.252
F of x is the integral from zero

00:04:34.293 --> 00:04:36.601
to x of f of t, d t.

00:04:37.346 --> 00:04:39.536
The letter t is a dummy variable, because

00:04:39.698 --> 00:04:41.004
x is already the upper limit.

00:04:41.768 --> 00:04:44.478
Here, that gives eight x minus x squared,

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:47.229
over sixteen, for x from zero to four.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:48.586
Check the ends.

00:04:49.212 --> 00:04:51.078
F of zero is zero, and F of

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.149
four is thirty two minus sixteen, over sixteen,

00:04:54.531 --> 00:04:55.012
which is one.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:58.261
And F of one is seven sixteenths, the

00:04:58.363 --> 00:04:59.344
area we just found.

00:05:00.256 --> 00:05:02.023
Going the other way takes one step.

00:05:02.691 --> 00:05:03.380
Differentiate.

00:05:04.226 --> 00:05:06.647
A variable has F of x equals x

00:05:06.708 --> 00:05:09.909
squared times three minus x, over four, for

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:11.430
x from zero to two.

00:05:12.274 --> 00:05:13.298
First check the ends.

00:05:14.003 --> 00:05:16.150
F of zero is zero, and F of

00:05:16.271 --> 00:05:19.121
two is four times one, over four, which

00:05:19.162 --> 00:05:19.482
is one.

00:05:20.287 --> 00:05:21.735
Expand it, and differentiate.

00:05:22.277 --> 00:05:24.704
The density is three x times two minus

00:05:24.885 --> 00:05:25.687
x, over four.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.535
Both factors are positive between zero and two,

00:05:28.877 --> 00:05:30.260
so f is never negative.

00:05:30.782 --> 00:05:33.087
And f is zero elsewhere, because the flat

00:05:33.128 --> 00:05:35.032
pieces of F have gradient zero.

00:05:35.656 --> 00:05:37.163
Here's a picture to hold on to.

00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:39.555
Think of the parcel tracker.

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.142
F is the chance it has arrived so

00:05:42.244 --> 00:05:45.370
far, and f is how fast that chance

00:05:45.451 --> 00:05:46.653
is building at x.

00:05:47.397 --> 00:05:48.931
Differentiate F to get f.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:51.366
Integrate f to get F.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:53.620
And by the end of the window, F

00:05:53.782 --> 00:05:54.970
reaches exactly one.

00:05:57.716 --> 00:05:58.119
Your turn.

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:01.091
A density is k times x plus one,

00:06:01.514 --> 00:06:03.820
for x from zero to two, and zero

00:06:03.981 --> 00:06:04.361
elsewhere.

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:07.654
Find k, then find the probability that X

00:06:07.796 --> 00:06:08.678
is greater than one.

00:06:09.342 --> 00:06:10.249
Pause here to answer.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:24.067
The total area is k times x squared

00:06:24.087 --> 00:06:26.431
over two plus x, from zero to two,

00:06:26.972 --> 00:06:27.674
which is four k.

00:06:28.516 --> 00:06:30.105
So k is one quarter.

00:06:31.027 --> 00:06:32.869
Then the probability that X is more than

00:06:33.109 --> 00:06:35.471
one is the integral from one to two

00:06:35.491 --> 00:06:37.552
of x plus one, over four.

00:06:38.414 --> 00:06:40.520
That's one quarter of four minus one and

00:06:40.541 --> 00:06:42.024
a half, which is five eighths.

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:43.895
Three quarters is wrong.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.194
That's the height of f at two, not

00:06:46.215 --> 00:06:46.678
an area.

00:06:48.251 --> 00:06:48.676
Last one.

00:06:49.528 --> 00:06:52.432
A continuous random variable has F of x

00:06:52.834 --> 00:06:55.999
equals four x minus x squared, over four,

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:57.962
for x from zero to two,

00:06:58.504 --> 00:07:01.328
with F equal to zero below zero, and

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:02.470
one above two.

00:07:03.253 --> 00:07:05.222
Find its probability density function.

00:07:05.869 --> 00:07:06.817
Pause here to answer.

00:07:18.218 --> 00:07:19.572
Differentiate the middle piece.

00:07:20.175 --> 00:07:22.757
Four minus two x, over four, is two

00:07:22.838 --> 00:07:25.619
minus x, over two, for x from zero

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:25.959
to two.

00:07:26.702 --> 00:07:27.687
It's never negative there.

00:07:28.452 --> 00:07:29.414
Outside that interval,

00:07:30.036 --> 00:07:32.321
f is zero, because the flat pieces of

00:07:32.563 --> 00:07:34.025
F have gradient zero.

00:07:34.829 --> 00:07:37.162
Saying f is one for x above two

00:07:37.345 --> 00:07:37.867
is wrong.

00:07:38.451 --> 00:07:40.729
The derivative of a constant is zero, not

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:40.910
one.

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:44.482
So the density is the gradient of F,

00:07:45.022 --> 00:07:47.044
probabilities are areas under it,

00:07:47.584 --> 00:07:49.546
and the total area is one.

00:07:50.409 --> 00:07:51.597
Next, a new question.

00:07:52.178 --> 00:07:54.160
Here's the density we found a moment ago,

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:57.523
three x times two minus x, over four.

00:07:58.245 --> 00:08:00.235
Where is X most likely to be?

00:08:01.079 --> 00:08:03.511
And where's the middle, with half the probability

00:08:03.672 --> 00:08:04.416
on each side?

00:08:07.528 --> 00:08:08.391
Here are the key notes.

00:08:08.794 --> 00:08:10.341
Pause the video if you need more time

00:08:10.383 --> 00:08:10.844
to copy them.
